<head>
<no><b>Part 2</b></no><heading guid="_71ba1e50-9cbb-4fc1-a994-908dd48090be"
id="pt.2-he"><b>Public holidays</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b6a53751-b3b7-43bc-a65d-57ec933af48b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_31244945-e532-4d62-9768-f5b9d8b52702"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Standard public holidays</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following public holidays are declared for
the whole State&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_61db3822-c5c9-471d-92ea-a2e839842639" id="sec.4-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_f80ceb88-d182-41b4-881e-be704ff70966"
id="sec.4-def.NewYearsDay"><b><i>New Year&#8217;s
Day</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on 1 January.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">When 1 January is a Saturday or Sunday, there is
to be an additional public holiday on the following
Monday.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d1a09ab8-b84f-4ad8-beea-2838121b7f98" id="sec.4-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_8900bca8-fb90-451d-9685-90df78a542ad"
id="sec.4-def.AustraliaDay"><b><i>Australia
Day</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on 26 January.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">When 26 January is a Saturday or Sunday, there is
to be no public holiday on that day and instead the following Monday is to be
a public holiday.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ab862ac2-83e8-42b3-af00-81dae35ab3db" id="sec.4-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_654db827-5689-41c2-9e35-a2f8e7ef4486"
id="sec.4-def.GoodFriday"><b><i>Good Friday</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on the Friday publicly observed as
Good Friday.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1e20a50a-b6a0-4aaa-9604-4759ee040442" id="sec.4-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_f6dbae6c-6aef-45b4-b855-67b9ad5b6146"
id="sec.4-def.EasterSaturday"><b><i>Easter
Saturday</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on the day after Good
Friday.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_05513c5d-3b02-4adc-9bd1-fc8373b0e809" id="sec.4-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_e4c5935a-d1bc-4b85-89ef-cd1173d006c7"
id="sec.4-def.EasterSunday"><b><i>Easter
Sunday</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on the Sunday following Good
Friday.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3825fa4a-e5dd-492a-b1e5-1f9096cad5c9" id="sec.4-para1.f">
<no>(f)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_6459125c-5349-4797-869b-069ff2ba2493"
id="sec.4-def.EasterMonday"><b><i>Easter
Monday</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on the Monday following Good
Friday.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_342345ef-c9f8-4868-8d13-d4107d5e3fd5" id="sec.4-para1.g">
<no>(g)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_75e12d00-0c05-4ed0-9b85-aeaf4e86c218"
id="sec.4-def.AnzacDay"><b><i>Anzac Day</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on 25 April.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_dec316d8-d577-4e43-baf1-cef8ca80e92d" id="sec.4-para1.h">
<no>(h)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_55a14789-1517-40c3-a22a-ae7d6c1a440f"
id="sec.4-def.KingsBirthday"><b><i>King&#8217;s
Birthday</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on the second Monday in
June.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1cc7c7e1-b4e2-486e-ba99-1cdc8abc8571" id="sec.4-para1.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_261a7191-adcc-4c19-a06f-f1e6504b29de"
id="sec.4-def.LabourDay"><b><i>Labour Day</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on the first Monday in
October.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b67c5642-328c-414f-9954-1fb175e09b1f" id="sec.4-para1.j">
<no>(j)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_1e29ee7b-8d6c-4879-a62a-980aac3585ea"
id="sec.4-def.ChristmasDay"><b><i>Christmas
Day</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on 25 December.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">When 25 December is a Saturday, there is to be an
additional public holiday on the following Monday.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">When 25 December is a Sunday, there is to be an
additional public holiday on the following Tuesday.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_bb4efe2f-babf-4bbd-b909-49d036f8e135" id="sec.4-para1.k">
<no>(k)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_5cab6ee4-cf96-4582-9d09-8b4407d258a9"
id="sec.4-def.BoxingDay"><b><i>Boxing Day</i></b></defterm></txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">Public holiday on 26 December.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">When 26 December is a Saturday, there is to be an
additional public holiday on the following Monday.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">When 26 December is a Sunday, there is to be an
additional public holiday on the following Tuesday.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 4:</b> Subst 2010 No
115, Sch 2.2. Am 2022 No 59, Sch 1.32.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_940d36e2-2629-4014-92c1-f563d25aa274"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_710aafe5-c97f-4023-8be9-fb18f9eca636"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Additional public holidays</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_07dc5dc9-7952-4fa4-b748-64132f06a7b0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister may by order published on the NSW
legislation website declare a specified day or part-day in a particular year
to be a public holiday. The order must be published at least 7 days before the
public holiday.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bef3a7cb-f9c1-46b2-b67c-bf3520af341c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The order can declare a public holiday for the
whole State or for a specified part of the State.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_04461117-6bdf-4e1d-b81d-dbf87018cbe6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister may by order published on the NSW
legislation website cancel a public holiday declared under this section. The
order must be published at least 7 days before the public
holiday.</txt></block></tier>

<note type="legtext" guid="_d841daca-a65d-4610-b2a4-06c9976c4d0d"
id="sec.5-note"><heading guid="_a7b9cb84-b435-48c4-b8b5-e06d7914cacd"
id="sec.5-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">Instead of cancelling an additional public
holiday declared under this section, the Minister can decide to substitute a
different day for the holiday under section 6.</txt></block></note>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1f1e312c-9f09-4919-9419-5e991e4314a8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_fa7d37b3-034e-45c9-94d9-f41f4b15ae63"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Substituted public holidays</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_537ad4d2-a6bf-4379-82b4-c1226cf9f8f7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister may by order published on the NSW
legislation website declare that a specified day or part-day in a particular
year (the <defterm type="definition"
guid="_cfd79b0c-d2e1-4ff1-9ab8-aee351ae8d39"
id="sec.6-def.substitutedday"><b><i>substituted day</i></b></defterm>) is to
be a public holiday in substitution for a specified day or part-day in that
year (the <defterm type="definition"
guid="_9c0e3eda-3f44-4cda-a9bc-6944b4fec0a8"
id="sec.6-def.originalday"><b><i>original day</i></b></defterm>) that would
otherwise be a public holiday in a particular year.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ac1c4942-a1d9-4fef-b84c-b5346670bf82"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The substituted day is then a public holiday and
the original day is not a public holiday.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_69c558e2-655a-4063-8048-404f14c91614"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The order must be published at least 7 days
before the earlier of the original day and the substituted day for the public
holiday.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3e99c5bb-fd61-4c37-83ab-f8cb7e3bcd1c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_4fe2bdc4-b408-457d-afeb-c1b866e69b45"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Employee entitlements on public
holidays</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1b6d9a12-bb06-4495-b459-1a3debd603c3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following provisions of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Fair Work Act
2009</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth apply as laws of New South Wales
to and in respect of employees and employers in the State&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ade39dda-480e-4fd3-86a3-5a145e76f34f" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1">
<block><txt break.before="1">section 114 (Entitlement to be absent from
employment on public holiday)</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_e51ec971-adf7-45fa-a70e-887ece505523" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1-oc.2">
<block><txt break.before="1">section 116 (Payment for absence on public
holiday)</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c3c1ce7b-48e4-4fbc-bae5-087f148a405c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section (and the provisions applying under
this section as laws of New South Wales) are deemed to be industrial
instruments for the purposes of Parts 1 (Breach of industrial instruments) and
2 (Recovery of remuneration and other amounts) of Chapter 7 of the <legref
refid="act-1996-017" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Industrial Relations Act
1996</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_de1bdc4f-84ed-4766-8ff9-2a09f58434d9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 3</b></no><heading guid="_a8c62376-3493-4b7a-9943-5b2990cdbae5"
id="pt.3-he"><b>Miscellaneous</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_08af6e11-d015-4c82-8ea2-18b5c2c273f2"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_ed02abb4-d563-4e5f-9cad-63ee9073df8c"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Local event days</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c7a7cd9b-a90f-4112-9043-dd5929917eab"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister may by order made at the request of
the council of a local government area declare a specified day or part-day to
be a local event day in the local government area or in a specified part of
the local government area.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3b466e74-0d46-4011-afb4-10d71f352010"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister is not to declare a local event day
unless satisfied that the day or part-day is, and will be observed as, a day
of special significance to the community in the area
concerned.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5415bc05-76fa-4ce0-85ec-0bc3fdb5afce"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The order declaring a local event day must be
published on the NSW legislation website at least 7 days before the local
event day.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_16fbaac0-9dde-471a-8cfb-14e2a664fbd1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The declaration of a local event day does not
make the local event day a public holiday.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7709e692-893e-441d-ab4d-874586ec732c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_7a3840d1-0ba6-4630-9a29-21b86630dcd3"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Delegations</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister may delegate the exercise of any
function of the Minister under this Act (other than this power of delegation)
to&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_5edb8485-3729-452f-bfaf-86e3f01b278b" id="sec.9-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the Director-General, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_967539ea-3449-4afa-858e-9723d8178b51" id="sec.9-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the holder of any position in the
Director-General&#8217;s Department that is prescribed by the
regulations.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_494689ee-4e5d-4d55-a01e-fb9340e1d830"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading guid="_cb9523aa-732a-4228-89b7-feb13561f5b9"
id="sec.10-he"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations, not
inconsistent with this Act, for or with respect to any matter that by this Act
is required or permitted to be prescribed or that is necessary or convenient
to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this
Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.11">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_282e0b63-cc7e-49f8-bd63-e45702222b32"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>11</no><heading guid="_7941e78d-56e6-418a-9c19-07e975f229a7"
id="sec.11-he"><b>Repeal of <legref refid="act-1912-043" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Banks and Bank Holidays Act
1912</i></name> No 43</legref></b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The <legref refid="act-1912-043" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Banks and Bank Holidays Act
1912</i></name></legref> is repealed.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.12">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2010aa9b-1ee1-45e5-bd67-0493cd41c3d8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>12</no><heading guid="_a27a1483-1d0e-44fa-a867-bdd19573f8e9"
id="sec.12-he"><b>Review of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.12-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_411d79d9-b78a-4946-b36f-73efb5d5c60f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister is to review this Act to determine
whether the policy objectives of the Act remain valid and whether the terms of
the Act remain appropriate for securing those
objectives.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.12-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c54f85b6-450d-4a41-ad66-4da780edf46f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The review is to be undertaken as soon as
possible after the period of 5 years from the date of assent to this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.12-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9dac2033-2c15-4d5e-99d9-ab0f35e8a85c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A report on the outcome of the review is to be
tabled in each House of Parliament within 12 months after the end of the
period of 5 years.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>
</content>


